# Generated by install-persistent.sh. Grants the active seat user access only to
# the selected input interfaces and gives each one a stable name, under a single
# directory, across reconnects. One rule line per configured device; the
# forwarder monitors every entry in /dev/input/wsf, so switching between mice
# mid-session keeps working. The lines match every action except remove, not
# just add: a later change/bind event on the same device (a Steam gamescope ->
# Plasma session switch reprocesses all of /sys/class/input, for instance)
# recomputes symlinks from the rules, and an add-only line would silently drop
# /dev/input/wsf while the mouse stays plugged in.
#
# The @DEVICE_MATCH@ placeholder carries the interface class of the selected
# node as well as its exact kernel name. Wheels are not only on mouse nodes:
# gaming keypads (Razer Tartarus) and unifying receivers put the wheel on a
# node udev classifies as a keyboard, which ID_INPUT_MOUSE would never match.
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", @DEVICE_MATCH@, TAG+="uaccess", SYMLINK+="input/wsf/%k"
